[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- Claims must be proportional to evidence. Choose verbs carefully — "demonstrate," "observe," and "hypothesize" mean different things.[39m                                                                [49m
[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- Every result needs: what was measured, on what data, the numbers, and what they mean.[39m                                                                                                               [49m
[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- Methodology must be specific enough to reproduce. Related work must be organized by theme, not a literature dump.[39m                                                                                   [49m
[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- State limitations honestly. Avoid both overclaiming and excessive hedging.[39m                                                                                                                          [49m
[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m</research_methodology>[39m                                                                                                                                                                               [49m
